<title>USA: Northern States restores King power plant.</title>
<headline>Northern States restores King power plant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern States Power Co said Monday its 581 megawatt Allen S. King coal fired power plant returned to full service over the weekend following a shutdown to repair a boiler tube leak.</p>
<p>The Oak Parks Heights, Minn., unit resumed full service on Saturday from an outage which began on Friday, Northern States said in a statement.</p>
<p>Oak Parks Heights is near Stillwater, Minn.</p>
<p>The King coal plant came on line in 1968.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
